(L2b) REACH of the SINGLE primary lattice L_n: which configs certified by t=1/n?
  (LRC holds for S as soon as no v_i ≡ 0 mod n; gcd-with-n is the obstruction)
  THEOREM: λ_n(S) >= 1/n  <=>  ∃k: v_i·k ≢ 0 (mod n) ∀i.  Certified by k=1 when
  all gcd(v_i,n)=1.  Below = exact via the residue criterion (no float).
==============================================================================
  n= 6: L_n single-lattice certifies  2348/5000 (47.0%);  uncertified need a non-floor pinch lattice
  n= 8: L_n single-lattice certifies  2265/5000 (45.3%);  uncertified need a non-floor pinch lattice
  n=12: L_n single-lattice certifies  2193/5000 (43.9%);  uncertified need a non-floor pinch lattice
  n=14: L_n single-lattice certifies  2186/5000 (43.7%);  uncertified need a non-floor pinch lattice
  n=15: L_n single-lattice certifies  2186/5000 (43.7%);  uncertified need a non-floor pinch lattice
  n=30: L_n single-lattice certifies  2197/5000 (43.9%);  uncertified need a non-floor pinch lattice

CONCLUSION: the signed/shell datum (v_i+v_j≡0 mod 2n-1) is a SECOND-gap binding
pair; it is dominated by the floor pinch (q=n) and CANNOT lower M below 1/n.
A signed zero-clock => an unsigned counterexample only if it is ALSO a floor
binding pair, i.e. v_i+v_j≡0 mod n — a DIFFERENT modulus. So the signed split of
the worry-set (AP vs V*) is invisible to M: a structural-reduction NO-GO.
